{"id":"mahabharata-3-255","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":255,"title":"पञ्चपञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 255 · The rout of Jayadratha's army","summary":{"en":"Jayadratha urges his men on, and the Pandavas cut down his warriors and the princes of Sauvira, strewing the field with headless bodies. Draupadi is rescued and brought back with Dhaumya; Jayadratha flees, and Yudhishthira tells Bhima and Arjuna to spare his life for the sake of Duhshala and Gandhari.","kn":"ಜಯದ್ರಥನು ತನ್ನವರನ್ನು ಹುರಿದುಂಬಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ಅವನ ಯೋಧರನ್ನೂ ಸೌವೀರ ರಾಜಕುಮಾರರನ್ನೂ ಕೆಡವಿ ರಣಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನು ತಲೆಯಿಲ್ಲದ ದೇಹಗಳಿಂದ ತುಂಬುತ್ತಾರೆ. ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯನ್ನು ಬಿಡಿಸಿ ಧೌಮ್ಯರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಕರೆತರಲಾಗುತ್ತದೆ; ಜಯದ್ರಥನು ಓಡುತ್ತಾನೆ, ದುಃಶಲೆ ಗಾಂಧಾರಿಯರಿಗಾಗಿ ಅವನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಬೇಡಿ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಭೀಮಾರ್ಜುನರಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"जयद्रथ अपने लोगों को उकसाता है, और पाण्डव उसके योद्धाओं और सौवीर राजकुमारों को काट गिराते हैं, रणभूमि बिना सिर के शवों से भर जाती है। द्रौपदी को छुड़ाकर धौम्य के साथ वापस लाया जाता है; जयद्रथ भागता है, और युधिष्ठिर भीम और अर्जुन से कहते हैं कि दुःशला और गान्धारी के लिए उसे जीवित छोड़ दें।","te":"జయద్రథుడు తనవారిని ప్రోత్సహిస్తాడు; పాండవులు అతని యోధులను, సౌవీర రాజకుమారులను కూల్చి రణభూమిని తలలేని శరీరాలతో నింపుతారు. ద్రౌపదిని విడిపించి ధౌమ్యునితో వెనక్కి తెస్తారు; జయద్రథుడు పారిపోతాడు, దుఃశల, గాంధారిల కోసం అతనిని చంపవద్దని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు భీమార్జునులకు చెబుతాడు.","ta":"ஜயத்ரதன் தன் ஆட்களைத் தூண்ட, பாண்டவர்கள் அவன் வீரர்களையும் ஸௌவீர இளவரசர்களையும் வீழ்த்திப் போர்க்களத்தைத் தலையற்ற உடல்களால் நிறைக்கிறார்கள். திரௌபதி மீட்கப்பட்டுத் தௌம்யருடன் திரும்பக் கொணரப்படுகிறாள்; ஜயத்ரதன் ஓட, துச்சலைக்காகவும் காந்தாரிக்காகவும் அவனைக் கொல்ல வேண்டாம் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் பீமனிடமும் அர்ஜுனனிடமும் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"ജയദ്രഥൻ സൈനികരെ പ്രോത്സാഹിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ വീരന്മാരെയും സൗവീരരാജകുമാരന്മാരെയും വെട്ടിവീഴ്ത്തുന്നു; തലയില്ലാത്ത ശരീരങ്ങൾകൊണ്ട് യുദ്ധഭൂമി നിറയുന്നു. ദ്രൗപദിയെ മോചിപ്പിച്ച് ധൗമ്യനോടൊപ്പം തിരികെ കൊണ്ടുവരുന്നു; ജയദ്രഥൻ ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു, ദുശ്ശളയെയും ഗാന്ധാരിയെയും ഓർത്ത് അവന്റെ ജീവൻ വെറുതെ വിടണമെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ഭീമനോടും അർജുനനോടും പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.255; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"द्रौपदीहरणपर्व","titleEn":"Draupadiharana Parva (Abduction of Draupadi)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"संतिष्ठत प्रहरत तूर्णं विपरिधावत ।\nइति स्म सैन्धवो राजा चोदयामास तान्नृपान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Stand firm, strike, run quickly at them!\" So the Sindhu king urged on those kings."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो घोरतरः शब्दो रणे समभवत्तदा ।\nभीमार्जुनयमान्दृष्ट्वा सैन्यानां सयुधिष्ठिरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a still more terrible noise arose in the battle as the soldiers saw Bhima, Arjuna, the twins and Yudhishthira."}},{"n":3,"text":"शिबिसिन्धुत्रिगर्तानां विषादश्चाप्यजायत ।\nतान्दृष्ट्वा पुरुषव्याघ्रान्व्याघ्रानिव बलोत्कटान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dismay came over the Shibis, Sindhus and Trigartas when they saw those tigers among men, like mighty tigers."}},{"n":4,"text":"हेमचित्रसमुत्सेधां सर्वशैक्यायसीं गदाम् ।\nप्रगृह्याभ्यद्रवद्भीमः सैन्धवं कालचोदितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up his all-iron mace, tall and decorated with gold, Bhima rushed at the Saindhava, driven by fate."}},{"n":5,"text":"तदन्तरमथावृत्य कोटिकाश्योऽभ्यहारयत् ।\nमहता रथवंशेन परिवार्य वृकोदरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kotikashya, covering the space between, attacked, surrounding Vrikodara with a great line of chariots."}},{"n":6,"text":"शक्तितोमरनाराचैर्वीरबाहुप्रचोदितैः ।\nकीर्यमाणोऽपि बहुभिर्न स्म भीमोऽभ्यकम्पत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though showered with spears, lances and iron arrows loosed by the arms of heroes, Bhima did not tremble."}},{"n":7,"text":"गजं तु सगजारोहं पदातींश्च चतुर्दश ।\nजघान गदया भीमः सैन्धवध्वजिनीमुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the front of the Saindhava's army, Bhima killed with his mace an elephant with its rider, and fourteen foot-soldiers."}},{"n":8,"text":"पार्थः पञ्चशताञ्शूरान्पार्वतीयान्महारथान् ।\nपरीप्समानः सौवीरं जघान ध्वजिनीमुखे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, seeking to reach the Sauvira, killed five hundred brave mountain-dwelling great warriors at the front of the force."}},{"n":9,"text":"राजा स्वयं सुवीराणां प्रवराणां प्रहारिणाम् ।\nनिमेषमात्रेण शतं जघान समरे तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king himself, in the blink of an eye, killed a hundred of the best fighters of the Suviras in that battle."}},{"n":10,"text":"ददृशे नकुलस्तत्र रथात्प्रस्कन्द्य खड्गधृक् ।\nशिरांसि पादरक्षाणां बीजवत्प्रवपन्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula was seen there, jumped down from his chariot with sword in hand, sowing the heads of the foot-soldiers like seed again and again."}},{"n":11,"text":"सहदेवस्तु संयाय रथेन गजयोधिनः ।\nपातयामास नाराचैर्द्रुमेभ्य इव बर्हिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva drove in his chariot and brought down elephant-fighters with iron arrows as one knocks peacocks from trees."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्त्रिगर्तः सधनुरवतीर्य महारथात् ।\nगदया चतुरो वाहान्राज्ञस्तस्य तदावधीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Trigarta king got down from his great chariot with his bow and killed the king's four horses with a mace."}},{"n":13,"text":"तमभ्याशगतं राजा पदातिं कुन्तिनन्दनः ।\nअर्धचन्द्रेण बाणेन विव्याधोरसि धर्मराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he came near on foot, King Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, pierced his chest with a crescent-headed arrow."}},{"n":14,"text":"स भिन्नहृदयो वीरो वक्त्राच्छोणितमुद्वमन् ।\nपपाताभिमुखः पार्थं छिन्नमूल इव द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His heart split, the hero, vomiting blood from his mouth, fell facing Arjuna like a tree cut at its root."}},{"n":15,"text":"इन्द्रसेनद्वितीयस्तु रथात्प्रस्कन्द्य धर्मराट् ।\nहताश्वः सहदेवस्य प्रतिपेदे महारथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Dharmaraja, with Indrasena as his second, jumped from his chariot, his horses killed, and took Sahadeva's great chariot."}},{"n":16,"text":"नकुलं त्वभिसंधाय क्षेमंकरमहामुखौ ।\nउभावुभयतस्तीक्ष्णैः शरवर्षैरवर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kshemankara and Mahamukha, aiming at Nakula, both showered him with sharp arrows from both sides."}},{"n":17,"text":"तौ शरैरभिवर्षन्तौ जीमूताविव वार्षिकौ ।\nएकैकेन विपाठेन जघ्ने माद्रवतीसुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they rained arrows like two monsoon clouds, the son of Madri killed each with a broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":18,"text":"त्रिगर्तराजः सुरथस्तस्याथ रथधूर्गतः ।\nरथमाक्षेपयामास गजेन गजयानवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Suratha, king of the Trigartas, standing at the pole of his chariot, had an elephant strike Nakula's chariot, being expert in elephant-driving."}},{"n":19,"text":"नकुलस्त्वपभीस्तस्माद्रथाच्चर्मासिपाणिमान् ।\nउद्भ्रान्तं स्थानमास्थाय तस्थौ गिरिरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fearless, Nakula, shield and sword in hand, left the chariot and stood like an unmoving mountain, in a position suited to such fighting."}},{"n":20,"text":"सुरथस्तं गजवरं वधाय नकुलस्य तु ।\nप्रेषयामास सक्रोधमभ्युच्छ्रितकरं ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Suratha angrily sent that best of elephants, trunk raised, to kill Nakula."}},{"n":21,"text":"नकुलस्तस्य नागस्य समीपपरिवर्तिनः ।\nसविषाणं भुजं मूले खड्गेन निरकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the elephant came close, Nakula cut off its tusked trunk at the base with his sword."}},{"n":22,"text":"स विनद्य महानादं गजः कङ्कणभूषणः ।\nपतन्नवाक्शिरा भूमौ हस्त्यारोहानपोथयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Roaring loudly, that elephant adorned with bracelets fell head down and crushed its riders."}},{"n":23,"text":"स तत्कर्म महत्कृत्वा शूरो माद्रवतीसुतः ।\nभीमसेनरथं प्राप्य शर्म लेभे महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having done that great deed, the brave son of Madri, a great warrior, reached Bhimasena's chariot and found shelter."}},{"n":24,"text":"भीमस्त्वापततो राज्ञः कोटिकाश्यस्य संगरे ।\nसूतस्य नुदतो वाहान्क्षुरेणापाहरच्छिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As King Kotikashya attacked in the battle, Bhima cut off the head of his charioteer, who was urging the horses, with a razor-headed arrow."}},{"n":25,"text":"न बुबोध हतं सूतं स राजा बाहुशालिना ।\nतस्याश्वा व्यद्रवन्संख्ये हतसूतास्ततस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That king did not realize his charioteer was dead, struck by the strong-armed hero; his horses, charioteer slain, bolted this way and that in the fight."}},{"n":26,"text":"विमुखं हतसूतं तं भीमः प्रहरतां वरः ।\nजघान तलयुक्तेन प्रासेनाभ्येत्य पाण्डवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandava Bhima, best of fighters, came up to him as he turned away, charioteer dead, and killed him with a spear fitted for the palm."}},{"n":27,"text":"द्वादशानां तु सर्वेषां सौवीराणां धनंजयः ।\nचकर्त निषितैर्भल्लैर्धनूंषि च शिरांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya cut down the bows and heads of all twelve Sauviras with sharp broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":28,"text":"शिबीनिक्ष्वाकुमुख्यांश्च त्रिगर्तान्सैन्धवानपि ।\nजघानातिरथः संख्ये बाणगोचरमागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great charioteer killed the Shibis, the chief Ikshvakus, the Trigartas and the Saindhavas who came within arrow range."}},{"n":29,"text":"सादिताः प्रत्यदृश्यन्त बहवः सव्यसाचिना ।\nसपताकाश्च मातङ्गाः सध्वजाश्च महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many were seen laid low by the left-handed archer, elephants with flags and great warriors with banners,"}},{"n":30,"text":"प्रच्छाद्य पृथिवीं तस्थुः सर्वमायोधनं प्रति ।\nशरीराण्यशिरस्कानि विदेहानि शिरांसि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"covering the earth over the whole battlefield, headless bodies and bodiless heads."}},{"n":31,"text":"श्वगृध्रकङ्ककाकोलभासगोमायुवायसाः ।\nअतृप्यंस्तत्र वीराणां हतानां मांसशोणितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dogs, vultures, herons, crows, kolas, bhasas, jackals and ravens feasted on the flesh and blood of the fallen heroes."}},{"n":32,"text":"हतेषु तेषु वीरेषु सिन्धुराजो जयद्रथः ।\nविमुच्य कृष्णां संत्रस्तः पलायनपरोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When those heroes had been killed, Jayadratha, king of the Sindhus, let go of Krishna and, terrified, thought only of fleeing."}},{"n":33,"text":"स तस्मिन्संकुले सैन्ये द्रौपदीमवतार्य वै ।\nप्राणप्रेप्सुरुपाधावद्वनं येन नराधमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that crowded army, the lowest of men put Draupadi down and, seeking his life, ran into the forest."}},{"n":34,"text":"द्रौपदीं धर्मराजस्तु दृष्ट्वा धौम्यपुरस्कृताम् ।\nमाद्रीपुत्रेण वीरेण रथमारोपयत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Draupadi with Dhaumya in front, Dharmaraja had her lifted into the chariot by the heroic son of Madri."}},{"n":35,"text":"ततस्तद्विद्रुतं सैन्यमपयाते जयद्रथे ।\nआदिश्यादिश्य नाराचैराजघान वृकोदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when Jayadratha had fled, Vrikodara struck the routed army with iron arrows, picking his targets."}},{"n":36,"text":"सव्यसाची तु तं दृष्ट्वा पलायन्तं जयद्रथम् ।\nवारयामास निघ्नन्तं भीमं सैन्धवसैनिकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The left-handed archer, seeing Jayadratha running, held back Bhima who was killing the Sindhu soldiers."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":37,"text":"यस्यापचारात्प्राप्तोऽयमस्मान्क्लेशो दुरासदः ।\nतमस्मिन्समरोद्देशे न पश्यामि जयद्रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not see in this battlefield Jayadratha, through whose wrongdoing this hard-to-bear misery came upon us."}},{"n":38,"text":"तमेवान्विष भद्रं ते किं ते योधैर्निपातितैः ।\nअनामिषमिदं कर्म कथं वा मन्यते भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look for him alone, good luck to you; what use is killing his warriors? This is a fruitless deed, or what do you think?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"इत्युक्तो भीमसेनस्तु गुडाकेशेन धीमता ।\nयुधिष्ठिरमभिप्रेक्ष्य वाग्मी वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by wise Gudakesha, Bhimasena looked at Yudhishthira and said, being eloquent:"}},{"n":40,"text":"हतप्रवीरा रिपवो भूयिष्ठं विद्रुता दिशः ।\nगृहीत्वा द्रौपदीं राजन्निवर्ततु भवानितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The enemies, their best heroes killed, have mostly fled in all directions. Take Draupadi and turn back from here, O king."}},{"n":41,"text":"यमाभ्यां सह राजेन्द्र धौम्येन च महात्मना ।\nप्राप्याश्रमपदं राजन्द्रौपदीं परिसान्त्वय ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the twins and the great-souled Dhaumya, go to the hermitage, king of kings, and comfort Draupadi."}},{"n":42,"text":"न हि मे मोक्ष्यते जीवन्मूढः सैन्धवको नृपः ।\nपातालतलसंस्थोऽपि यदि शक्रोऽस्य सारथिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The foolish Saindhava king will not escape me alive, even if he were in the depths of the netherworld with Indra as his charioteer.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":43,"text":"न हन्तव्यो महाबाहो दुरात्मापि स सैन्धवः ।\nदुःशलामभिसंस्मृत्य गान्धारीं च यशस्विनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mighty-armed one, he must not be killed, wicked though that Saindhava is, remembering Duhshala and the famous Gandhari."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा द्रौपदी भीममुवाच व्याकुलेन्द्रिया ।\nकुपिता ह्रीमती प्राज्ञा पती भीमार्जुनावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing this, Draupadi, her senses upset, angry and modest and wise, said to both her husbands, Bhima and Arjuna:"}},{"n":45,"text":"कर्तव्यं चेत्प्रियं मह्यं वध्यः स पुरुषाधमः ।\nसैन्धवापसदः पापो दुर्मतिः कुलपांसनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you must do what pleases me, that lowest of men must be killed: the Saindhava rubbish, the sinful, evil-minded stain of his family."}},{"n":46,"text":"भार्याभिहर्ता निर्वैरो यश्च राज्यहरो रिपुः ।\nयाचमानोऽपि संग्रामे न स जीवितुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who abducts another's wife, who is without enmity, or an enemy who seizes a kingdom, does not deserve to live in a battle even if he begs.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"इत्युक्तौ तौ नरव्याघ्रौ ययतुर्यत्र सैन्धवः ।\nराजा निववृते कृष्णामादाय सपुरोहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, those two tigers among men went where the Saindhava was. King Yudhishthira turned back with Krishna and the priest."}},{"n":48,"text":"स प्रविश्याश्रमपदं व्यपविद्धबृसीघटम् ।\nमार्कण्डेयादिभिर्विप्रैरनुकीर्णं ददर्श ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering the hermitage, where the water jars and seats had been thrown about, he saw it filled with brahmins led by Markandeya."}},{"n":49,"text":"द्रौपदीमनुशोचद्भिर्ब्राह्मणैस्तैः समागतैः ।\nसमियाय महाप्राज्ञः सभार्यो भ्रातृमध्यगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The very wise man, with his wife and surrounded by his brothers, met the brahmins who gathered grieving for Draupadi."}},{"n":50,"text":"ते स्म तं मुदिता दृष्ट्वा पुनरभ्यागतं नृपम् ।\nजित्वा तान्सिन्धुसौवीरान्द्रौपदीं चाहृतां पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were delighted to see the king return, having defeated the Sindhu-Sauvira forces and brought Draupadi back."}},{"n":51,"text":"स तैः परिवृतो राजा तत्रैवोपविवेश ह ।\nप्रविवेशाश्रमं कृष्णा यमाभ्यां सह भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded by them the king sat down there; and Krishna, the lovely woman, entered the hermitage with the twins."}},{"n":52,"text":"भीमार्जुनावपि श्रुत्वा क्रोशमात्रगतं रिपुम् ।\nस्वयमश्वांस्तुदन्तौ तौ जवेनैवाभ्यधावताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima and Arjuna, hearing that the enemy was only a krosha away, themselves lashed their horses and sped on swiftly."}},{"n":53,"text":"इदमत्यद्भुतं चात्र चकार पुरुषोऽर्जुनः ।\nक्रोशमात्रगतानश्वान्सैन्धवस्य जघान यत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna did this very wonderful thing: he killed the Saindhava's horses a krosha away."}},{"n":54,"text":"स हि दिव्यास्त्रसंपन्नः कृच्छ्रकालेऽप्यसंभ्रमः ।\nअकरोद्दुष्करं कर्म शरैरस्त्रानुमन्त्रितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Equipped with divine weapons, steady even at a time of danger, he did a hard deed with arrows empowered by weapon-mantras."}},{"n":55,"text":"ततोऽभ्यधावतां वीरावुभौ भीमधनंजयौ ।\nहताश्वं सैन्धवं भीतमेकं व्याकुलचेतसम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two heroes, Bhima and Dhananjaya, ran after the lone, frightened Saindhava, whose horses were dead and mind confused."}},{"n":56,"text":"सैन्धवस्तु हतान्दृष्ट्वा तथाश्वान्स्वान्सुदुःखितः ।\nदृष्ट्वा विक्रमकर्माणि कुर्वाणं च धनंजयम् ।\nपलायनकृतोत्साहः प्राद्रवद्येन वै वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Saindhava, deeply pained to see his horses killed and seeing Dhananjaya's feats of valor, was moved to flee and ran into the forest."}},{"n":57,"text":"सैन्धवं त्वभिसंप्रेक्ष्य पराक्रान्तं पलायने ।\nअनुयाय महाबाहुः फल्गुनो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Saindhava putting on speed in flight, mighty-armed Phalguna followed and said:"}},{"n":58,"text":"अनेन वीर्येण कथं स्त्रियं प्रार्थयसे बलात् ।\nराजपुत्र निवर्तस्व न ते युक्तं पलायनम् ।\nकथं चानुचरान्हित्वा शत्रुमध्ये पलायसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"With such valor how do you seek a woman by force? Turn back, prince; flight does not suit you. How can you abandon your followers and run away among enemies?\""}},{"n":59,"text":"इत्युच्यमानः पार्थेन सैन्धवो न न्यवर्तत ।\nतिष्ठ तिष्ठेति तं भीमः सहसाभ्यद्रवद्बली ।\nमा वधीरिति पार्थस्तं दयावानभ्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though Arjuna called out thus, the Saindhava did not turn back. Bhima, the strong, suddenly rushed at him crying \"Stop, stop!\" and compassionate Arjuna said to him, \"Do not kill him.\""}}]}]}